tion stage within the Faster R-CNN framework, responsible for classifying the region proposals generated by the RPN. ; A two-stage object detection framework, where the second stage classifies the region proposals generated by the RPN. ; A region-based convolutional neural network used for object detection, forming a branch within the Faster R-CNN framework.\n', 'Name:KITTI DATASET\nDescription:A dataset used for car detection. ; A dataset used for object detection, particularly for autonomous driving applications. ; A dataset used for object detection, specifically for car detection, and evaluation of the Faster R-CNN algorithm. ; A dataset used for training and evaluating car detection models, with images of 1295 x 375 resolution. ; A dataset used for evaluating car detection performance. ; A dataset used for training and evaluating car detection models.\n', "Name:ALEXNET\nDescription:A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) architecture. ; A shallow convolutional neural network architecture that provides high accuracy on the detection task. ; A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) architecture, relevant to the study of car detection using Faster R-CNN. ; A Convolutional Neural Network architecture, used as a backbone in Faster R-CNN for feature extraction. ; A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) architecture. The text mentions specific layer sizes (e.g., 6x6 in pool5) relevant to the study's focus on architectural variations and input image scaling. ; A Convolutional Neural Network architecture used in Faster R-CNN for object detection. ; A Convolutional Neural Network architecture used within the Faster R-CNN framework for feature extraction and object detection. ; A Convolutional Neural Network architecture, used for feature extraction, and compared with VGG16. ; A Convolutional Neural Network architecture used for image classification and object detection, explored in the context of Faster R-CNN for car detection. ; A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) architecture used in the study, specifically its performance is compared against VGG16. ; A Convolutional Neural Network architecture used in Faster R-CNN for object detection, and compared with VGG16 in this study. ; A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) architecture used in Faster R-CNN for car detection, as described in the priming summary. The text unit mentions its use with conv5 features and different input image resolutions. ; A convolutional neural network architecture used as a base for the Faster R-CNN model. ; A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) architecture used in Faster R-CNN configurations for car detection. The text mentions its performance with context windows and different anchor box selection schemes, and its inference time.\n"]split_entities: text_tokens=2579, instructions_tokens=500, budget_for_entities=6921, number_of_entities=58, avg_entity_tokens=71, max_entities=97, num_groups=1, entities_per_group=[58]
